<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 12-AUG.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS - WSC - 12-AUG.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Winnie is approaching the northern Mariana Islands. Typhoon warnings are up for Saipan, Tinian, Anatahan, Alamagan, Pagan, and Agrihan. Winnie has 120 mph winds and is expected to continue to intensify as it moves west northwestward across the islands, about 200 miles north of Guam, during Tuesday. Wind damage, storm surge flooding, and heavy rain with flooding will likely occur.  </p>
<p>Nothing further at this time.</p>
</text>
